A drainage channel has a cross-section bounded by ground level $y=0$ and the curve $y=x^2-9$. Both coordinates are measured in metres. Find the cross-sectional area.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.65cm,y=0.25cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},draw=black,text=black]
\definecolor{mathsmapLightGreen}{HTML}{DCEBE0}
\fill[fill=mathsmapLightGreen] (-3,0) -- plot[domain=-3:3,samples=61] (\x,{\x*\x-9}) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-3.8,0)--(3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-10.5)--(0,2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-3.3:3.3,samples=61] (\x,{\x*\x-9});
\path (-3,0) node[above] {$-3$} (3,0) node[above] {$3$};
\path (0,-9) node[below left] {$-9$};
\path (0,1) node[above left] {ground level};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

An arch window is $4$ metres high and $4$ metres wide. Its upper boundary is $y=4\cos\left(\frac{\pi x}{4}\right)$ and its sill is $y=0$, for $-2\leq x\leq2$. Find the glass area, correct to one decimal place.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.65cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},draw=black,text=black]
\definecolor{mathsmapLightGreen}{HTML}{DCEBE0}
\fill[fill=mathsmapLightGreen] (-2,0) -- plot[domain=-2:2,samples=61] (\x,{4*cos(45*\x)}) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-2.7,0)--(2.7,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.5)--(0,4.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-2:2,samples=61] (\x,{4*cos(45*\x)});
\path (-2,0) node[below] {$-2$} (2,0) node[below] {$2$};
\path (0,4) node[above left] {$4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
